# Pages and layouts

- `page.tsx` / `layout.tsx` = minimal scaffolding only
- Logic, queries, and UI live in `modules/*/components/`
- Module page component is always named `Page` (path already scopes the domain: `modules/example/components/Page.tsx`)
- The App Router file only wires it (thin default export)

## Auth

Gate the shell once in the route layout:

- `app/dashboard/layout.tsx` → `requireAuth()` (any signed-in user)
- `app/admin/layout.tsx` → `requireAdmin()`
- `proxy.ts` redirects unauthenticated and wrong-role traffic
- APIs use `procedure_protected` / `procedure_admin`

Use `PageLayout` in the module component for width/padding; it is layout chrome, not an auth gate.

```tsx
// app/dashboard/layout.tsx
export default async function DashboardLayout(props: PropsWithChildren) {
  await requireAuth();
  return props.children;
}

// app/admin/layout.tsx
export default async function AdminLayout(props: PropsWithChildren) {
  await requireAdmin();
  return props.children;
}

// app/dashboard/page.tsx
import { Page } from '@/modules/example/components/Page';

export default function DashboardPage() {
  return <Page />;
}
```

## Query handling belongs in module components

```tsx
// modules/example/components/ExampleDashboard.tsx
export function ExampleDashboard() {
  const itemsQuery = useSessionQuery(service_example.queries.list());

  if (itemsQuery.data) return (/* render */);
  if (itemsQuery.isError) return (/* error */);
  return (/* skeleton */);
}
```

## JSX conditionals

- Optional UI: `condition && <Node />` — not `condition ? <Node /> : null`
